"Qvortrup","name":"Qvortrup, Ane","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Merete","key":"wibergpedh","last":"Wiberg","name":"Wiberg, Merete","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gerd","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Gerd","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mikala","key":"hansbølpedh","last":"Hansbøl","name":"Hansbøl, Mikala","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788776748760"],"pages":"21-37","place":"Odense","publisher":"Syddansk Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"On the definition of learning"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8ad8016a-585b-424a-ad63-78ff49ac895c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"What should we demand of a definition of 'learning'?","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-613010","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In the article, we have shown how, especially in the Denmark, broad concepts of constructivism and socio-cultural learning theories seem to have replaced education theory and didactics as conceptual framework reasoning on teaching and choices of design in the Scholarship of Teaching and Learning in Higher Education. We have illustrated how and why didactic theory and practice cannot be deduced from learning theoretical concepts and have discussed possible consequences of the displacement towards learning theory. Finally, we have argued that both learning theories and didactics are fundamental for systematic reflection of teaching and learning and cannot be replaced by each other. Empirical research gives strong arguments for a variety of methods and a clear eye for the students’ learning process as a whole, and we do not question the relevance of a student-oriented approach in the sense that teaching is planned and carried out with a clear focus on the pedagogical significance and students learning. But we do question student-oriented approaches as the only methodological dimension in teaching. In line with (Barr & Tagg, 1995, p. 14) our credo is that teachers must chose “whatever approaches serves best to prompt learning of particular knowledge by particular students.”. Furthermore, we do question the idea that learning theory can replace didactics and that the education system benefits from the current learnification. The exchange of the language of teaching with the language of learning is not just a simple replacement of one word with another without significance of the meaning. On the contrary, it deprives us a systematic framework for reflection on teaching, at the risk of becoming blind for the many didactic decisions that we make whenever we try to design “learning environments” and “learning activities”. The risk points in two directions: Either we forget the role of schooling and teaching and leaves the student with the responsibly of designing educational relevant activities. In this case, students become responsible not only for their own learning but for own teaching. Or we might be seduced to think that we as teachers actually plan – or even steer and observe – students learning and risk to neglect “the educative difference of matter and meaning and a strong conviction that teaching and learning are necessarily autonomous activities” (Hopmann, 2007, p. 121). We will designate the first risk as “the students as his/hers own didactician” (Keiding, 2008) and the second as “trivialization” (Luhmann, 2002b, p. 77ff) and in line with Keiding and Qvortrup (2014) uphold that neither is compatible with quality teaching and hence not with the function of a Scholarship in Teaching and Learning in Higher Education.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Qvortrup, Ane","Keiding, Tina Bering"],"cuid":["S02-094.83-025392"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Didactics","Didaktik","Learning theory","Læringsteori","Scholarship of Teaching and Learning in Higher Education"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the mistake to mistake learning theory with didactics","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-094.83-025392","ids":["au-aeb987b2-3e6a-462a-b23a-1dba10769833","sdu-3071daa7-3712-48eb-84ec-166be702cd08"],"keyword":["Didactics","Didaktik","Learning Theory","Læringsteori","Scholarship of Teaching and Learning in Higher Education"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-2-E090C4D3FA23447F65A83D931F06937E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture, Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Centre for Teaching Development and Digital Media, Centre for Teaching Development and Digital Media - Team for Didaktisk udvikling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ane","key":"qvortruppau","last":"Qvortrup","locid":"e888627a-aeb0-437b-991d-57505f52659f","name":"Qvortrup, Ane","orcid":"0000-0002-2110-0575","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Bering","key":"keidingpau","last":"Keiding","locid":"c4a894a0-be6c-4583-8ef8-1c0f3ced5dea","name":"Keiding, Tina Bering","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ane","key":"qvortruppedh","last":"Qvortrup","name":"Qvortrup, Ane","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Merete","key":"wibergpedh","last":"Wiberg","name":"Wiberg, Merete","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gerd","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Gerd","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mikala","key":"hansbølpedh","last":"Hansbøl","name":"Hansbøl, Mikala","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788776748760"],"pages":"163-187","place":"Odense","publisher":"Syddansk Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"On the Definition of Learning"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-aeb987b2-3e6a-462a-b23a-1dba10769833","sdu-3071daa7-3712-48eb-84ec-166be702cd08"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The mistake to mistake learning theory with didactics","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.83-025392","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
