{"abstract":"The research project “Educational cultures and serious games on a global market place” (2009-2011) dealt with the challenge of the digital learning environment and hence it’s educational development space always existing outside the present space and hence scope of activities. With a reference to Vygotsky’s concept of the zone of proximal development, Hasse’s concept of the relational zone of proximal development, inspiration from actor-network-theoretical conceptualizations of the ontological multiplicity and fluidity of technology, and empirical studies of the emerging circulations and establishments of the virtual universe called Mingoville.com, the research shows a need to include in researchers’ conceptualizations of digital learning environments and resources, their shifting materialities and platformations and hence emerging (often unpredictable) agencies and educational development spaces. Keywords: Fluidity, digital learning environment, digital learning resource, educational development space","author_count":1,"contributors":["Hansbøl, Mikala"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-552998"],"event":{"end":"2012-04-27","place":"Emdrup, dk","start":"2012-04-25","title":"DESIGNS FOR LEARNING 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Didactics","It didaktisk design","Læringsspil","digitale læringsmiljøer"],"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the fluidities of digital learning environments and resources opening up their educational development spaces","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://pure.au.dk/portal/files/45188015/DfL2012_Conference_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-552998","ids":["pha-047fd57b-2142-456f-b612-c40cf50584c0"],"keyword":["didactics","didaktiske udviklingsrum","digitale læringsmiljøer","it-didaktisk design","læringsspil"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-8293D86310D8EF6E1C166E52A540DBFF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Ledelses og Fællesfunktioner (LOF), Forskning og Innovation, Ledelse og fællesfunktioner Sorø"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikala","key":"hansbølpau","last":"Hansbøl","locid":"78cb8a07-8acc-48b5-899b-2e5ef94d1028","name":"Hansbøl, Mikala","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788799532803"],"pages":"32-35","place":"Danmark","status":"p","title":"Ukendt"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College Absalon","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-047fd57b-2142-456f-b612-c40cf50584c0"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"The fluidities of digital learning environments and resources : opening up their educational development spaces","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-552998","year":"2012","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"  This paper takes its point of departure in a language project, which is a subproject under the larger ongoing (2007-2011) research project Serious Games on a Global Market Place. The language project follows how the virtual universe known as Mingoville ( http://www.mingoville.com/ ) becomes an actor in English education for beginners. The virtual universe provides an online environment for students beginning to learn English in schools and at home. This paper will focus on the shifting ontologies of Mingoville and teaching and learning situations in beginners' English. This paper takes its point of departure in neither Mingoville as part of the media ecologies of the classroom, nor in the epistemological ramifications of Mingoville. Instead, it suggests that opening up the shifting ontologies of Mingoville (i.e. what mediates Mingoville and its relationships with doing beginners English) may offer a different and useful approach to understanding how Mingoville becomes a multiple actor. It reveals that such an actor both influences, and is influenced by, manifold constitutive entanglements involved in organizing English teaching and learning activities for beginners. Theoretically and methodologically, the paper, the empirical gatherings and analysis, are inspired by science and technology studies (STS) and actor-network-theory (ANT). The arguments and descriptions provided throughout the paper will focus on the shifting ontologies of Mingoville as it moves into, and out of, different teaching and learning situations of English for beginners. Keywords: Entanglement approach, relational ontology, serious games, teaching and learning English for beginners, educational technology research","author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansbøl, Mikala","Meyer, Bente Tobiesen"],"cuid":["S02-098.74-025133"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["ANT Actor Network Theory","ANT 